  "summary": "Both previous analyses correctly identify the core bug (failed items permanently stuck in `_auto_plan_queued`) but miss two critical additional failure modes. First, `_run_ideating_async` and `_run_plan_async` share `@work(exclusive=True, group=\"plan\")`, meaning Textual will silently cancel a running worker if a new one starts in the same group — if auto-plan picks an ideating item and then triggers a plan-inbox item before the first completes, the cancelled worker never calls `_on_plan_done`, permanently orphaning that slug in `_auto_plan_queued`. Second, the `_handle_rate_limit` path (lines 3813-3815 and 3750-3752) sets the shared cooldown but never discards the slug either, so rate-limited items are doubly stuck: blocked by `_rate_limit_until` AND permanently lodged in `_auto_plan_queued`. Contribution 2's per-slug failure counter is over-engineered for local failures (corrupted JSON fails before any API call, so retrying every 60s via `AUTO_RUN_INTERVAL` costs nothing); the simpler fix is: (1) add `self._auto_plan_queued.discard(feature.slug)` to the `finally` blocks of both `_run_ideating_async` and `_run_plan_async`, (2) split `_rate_limit_until` into separate plan/impl timestamps so rate-limiting one mode doesn't stall the other, and (3) either separate ideating and planning into different Textual work groups or add a queue so exclusive-group cancellation doesn't silently orphan slugs."
